  "body": "Follow-up to #63, from benchmarking the read paths. Compression turned out to be a mixed result, and search was the bad half.\n\n## Measured on 4,000 real requests\n\n| operation | inline | compressed | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `stats()` aggregate | 311 ms | **53 ms** | 5.8x faster |\n| list page of 50 | 18 ms | 41 ms | 2.2x slower |\n| detail read x50 | 150 ms | 198 ms | 1.3x slower |\n| search, selective | 1,443 ms | **9,056 ms** | 6.3x slower |\n\nThe aggregate got much faster because it no longer walks overflow pages — that is the dashboard's main query, so it is the one that mattered most. Search got much slower because the predicate decompressed *and* JSON-parsed every row.\n\n## The fix\n\nMost rows do not match, and for those the JSON parse and UTF-8 decode are pure waste. JSON encoding only rewrites `\"`, `\\` and control characters, so a needle containing none of them appears in the stored blob byte for byte — meaning **absent from the encoded bytes proves absent from the decoded text**.\n\nThat makes a bytes-level test a sound *rejection* filter. It is deliberately not used as an acceptance test, because it can match a key name or structural punctuation, so a hit is still verified against decoded text. A needle that JSON would escape skips the filter entirely.\n\n| search term | inline | compressed | | matches |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| selective miss | 1,443 ms | **1,919 ms** | 1.3x slower | 0 |\n| rare word | 1,578 ms | 1,906 ms | 1.2x slower | 1 |\n| common word (`the`) | 383 ms | 5,493 ms | 14.3x slower | 3,991 |\n\nSelective search went from 6.3x slower to 1.3x. A term matching 99.8% of rows is unchanged and inherently so — when nearly everything matches, the decode is the work rather than the waste.\n\n## Correctness\n\nThree tests pin what could go quietly wrong:\n\n- needles containing quotes, backslashes and newlines still match (they skip the filter)\n- structural fragments like `\",\"`, `{\"i\":`, `\"o\"` match nothing\n- an inline store and a compressed store return **the same row ids** for the same searches\n\nLocal suite 3,395 passed, with the 6 known PowerShell installer failures that predate this branch.\n\nPATCH: 4.45.0 → 4.45.1.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
